dialect protocol
protocol stdio.semio.video.mutations
version 1
schema stdio.semio.video
start body
framing record

# Video wave: REAL binary op frame, replacing the old `print_op().into_bytes()` text-as-binary
# shortcut (`🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s old `OpBinary::encode_op`). `SemioVideoMutation` is a
# genuine data-carrying enum whose variants embed nested `SemioVideoStream`/`SemioVideoSample`/
# `SemioVideoSnapshot` payloads — no `dsl::DslField` impl exists for any of them (hand-rolled per
# this subset's own `🔺️diff`/`🧬️mutations` convention), so the generic derive-based
# `format u8 | ordinal varint | record body` layout doesn't apply. Handcrafted instead: `format u8`
# (`OP_BINARY_FORMAT` convention) + `tag u8` (the `SemioVideoMutation` variant ordinal,
# `🧬️mutations/🦀️.rs`'s `OP_KEYWORDS`/`variant_ordinal`, same 0-8 ordering as
# `parse_semio_video_mutation`'s keyword match) as two REAL fixed fields, then the variant's own
# `key=value ...` argument payload as one opaque trailing `bytes` chain — the same honest boundary
# the sibling `../../🔺️diff/💾️binary/📡️.protocol.semio` uses.
header fixed 2
field format u8
field tag u8

chain payload bytes
